"Lighthouse: the pulse geometry is exact for a beam of half width ρ around each magnetic pole: cos θ = cos α cos ζ + sin α sin ζ cos φ, a pulse while θ < ρ (Lorimer and Kramer {#}). The beam shape across its width is schematic.",
"Spin down: magnetic dipole braking in vacuum with I = {#}³⁸ kg m² and R = {#} km, as the ATNF Pulsar Catalogue assumes: Ė = {#}π²IṖ/P³, τ = P/{#}Ṗ, B = {#} × {#}¹⁵ √(PṖ) T. Real pulsars brake with indices below {#}.",
